  "worked_solution": "We note that $b=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nThe equation has the denominators $36b$ and $12{b}^{2}.$ So first, we find the least common multiple (or $\\text{LCM}$) of the denominators. We find that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(36b,12{b}^{2})=36{b}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $36{b}^{2},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5b+8}{12{b}^{2}} & =-\\frac{12}{36b}+\\frac{4b+8}{12{b}^{2}} \\\\ 36{b}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{5b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) & =36{b}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{12}{36b}+\\frac{4b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) \\\\ 36{b}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{5b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) & =36{b}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{12}{36b})+36{b}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{4b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) \\\\ 3\\cdot 12{b}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{5b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) & =b\\cdot 36b\\cdot (-\\frac{12}{36b})+3\\cdot 12{b}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{4b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) \\\\ 3\\cdot \\cancel{12{b}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{5b+8}{\\cancel{12{b}^{2}}}) & =b\\cdot \\cancel{36b}\\cdot (-\\frac{12}{\\cancel{36b}})+3\\cdot \\cancel{12{b}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{4b+8}{\\cancel{12{b}^{2}}}) \\\\ 3(5b+8) & =-12b+3(4b+8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $b,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(5b+8) & =-12b+3(4b+8) \\\\ 15b+24 & =-12b+12b+24 \\\\ 15b+24 & =24 \\\\ 15b & =24-24 \\\\ 15b & =0 \\\\ b & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $b=0$ as a solution. Since $b=0,$ we conclude that there is no solution.",
